 "name": "German"}, "word": "ermöglichen"}, {"language": {"code": "he", "name": "Hebrew"}, "word": "אפשר"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "lehetővé tesz"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive, obsolete) To praise; to approve of; hence, to sanction.", "tags": ["obsolete", "transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Truly ye bear witness that ye allow the deeds of your fathers", "reference": "1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Luke 11:48:"}, {"text": "We commend his pains, condemn his pride, allow his life, approve his learning.", "reference": "1842, Thomas Fuller, Church History of Britain:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) To sanction; to invest; to entrust.", "tags": ["obsolete"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Therefore so please thee to return with us,\nAnd of our Athens—thine and ours—to take\nThe captainship, thou shalt be met with thanks,\nAllow'd with absolute power, and thy good name\nLive with authority. So soon we shall drive back\nOf Alcibiades the approaches wild,\nWho, like a boar too savage, doth root up\nHis country's peace.", "reference": "1623, William Shakespeare, The Life of Timon of Athens:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive, obsolete) To like; to be suited or pleased with.", "tags": ["obsolete", "transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "How allow you the model of these clothes?", "reference": "1632, Philip Massinger, Nathan Field, The Fatal Dowry, act 4, scene 1:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(law, transitive) To decide (a request) in favour of the party who raised it; to grant victory to a party regarding (a request).", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": ["to allow an objection", "to allow an appeal"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonym